# Per-Dockerfile ignore list for Dockerfile.default.localsrc, which is the ONE image that
# builds Tika from a local checkout instead of cloning a pinned commit. BuildKit prefers
# "<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore" over the context-root .dockerignore, so this file exists
# solely to NOT exclude .tika-src.
#
# The root .dockerignore excludes .tika-src/ to keep ~0.5 GB off the wire on every ordinary
# build. That is right for every other image and fatal for this one: `COPY .tika-src` against
# an excluded path fails outright with
#
#     failed to compute cache key: "/.tika-src": not found
#
# which is what this Dockerfile did from the moment .tika-src/ was added to the root list.
#
# BuildKit REPLACES the root list rather than merging, so every other exclusion has to be
# repeated here. Keep this file in sync with .dockerignore -- minus .tika-src/.
#
# `.git` excludes only the repo root's .git; the checkout's own .tika-src/.git is a
# different path and is still copied, which is what lets the provenance step record a real
# commit rather than "unknown".
.git
.tika-fixed/
.tika-baseline/
worker_jvm/target/
**/__pycache__/
.venv/
*.ext4
